 "markdown": "## Summary\nAdd a secondary \"Home\" action button to the page header, placed before the existing \"Next\" button, that navigates the user to the home page.\n\n## How it works today\nThe page is an `oj-sp-general-overview-page` whose `primary-action` renders a single \"Next\" button; clicking it fires `$listeners.nextToCatalog`, which runs `NavigateToCatalogChain`. There is no \"Home\" button today.\n\n## What changes\n`oj-sp-general-overview-page` supports a `secondary-action` slot/attribute rendered beside the primary action. I'll add a \"Home\" secondary action wired to a new `goHome` listener and a new `GoHomeChain` that navigates to the home page.\n\n## The change\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/project-create-request-page.html` — add `secondary-action` + `on-sp-secondary-action` for a \"Home\" button on the overview page component.\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/project-create-request-page.json` — declare the `goHome` event listener calling `GoHomeChain`.\n- `webApps/vbredwoodapp/flows/customer-portal/pages/project-create-request-page-chains/GoHomeChain.js` — new chain that navigates to the app's home page.\n\n## After the change\n- On the Create Equipment Request page header, the user will see a \"Home\" button immediately before the \"Next\" button.\n- Clicking \"Home\" takes the user to the application home page.\n- \"Next\" still behaves exactly as before.\n\n## Risks\n- The home navigation target must match how this app routes \"home\". I used the app's default/root page via `navigateToPage`; if the app uses a different home flow/page name this must be adjusted (see Questions).\n- No other page shares this new chain or listener.\n\n## How to test\n1. Open `/vp/shell/customer-portal/project-create-request`.\n2. Confirm a \"Home\" button appears before \"Next\" in the page header.\n3. Click \"Home\" — you should land on the application home page.\n4. Click \"Next\" and confirm it still proceeds to the catalog as before.\n\n## Questions\nI need to confirm the exact home destination. I navigated to the app root/dashboard using the shell's default. If \"Home\" should target a specific named flow/page (e.g. a dashboard page), tell me the flow and page id and I'll point `GoHomeChain` there. The edits below assume navigating to the application's default (home) page is acceptable.",
 "questions": "I need to confirm the exact home destination. I navigated to the app root/dashboard using the shell's default. If \"Home\" should target a specific named flow/page (e.g. a dashboard page), tell me the flow and page id and I'll point `GoHomeChain` there. The edits below assume navigating to the application's default (home) page is acceptable.",
